    narr:narration """The call opens with [a self-initiated correction, offered at the top rather than buried](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_1), which the chair invites and then presses on. The substance is a [retraction of a two-week soak estimate, asked to be struck from the plan](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_3), grounded in [a re-analysis of the Dockside exception-queue logs](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_5) prompted by a colleague's one-site-one-season comment. The key finding: [the retired weekly reconciliation job, not site behaviour, produced the nine-day flattening](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_7). From that, [a revised one-week soak is proposed](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_9), while [the sequential one-site-at-a-time rollout is explicitly confirmed unchanged](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_10). The chair [ratifies the superseded timeline for the record](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_20) and [directs the re-analysis be written up for the steering group](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_21), with [the write-up committed same-day](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_22). The recovered time is [allocated to the Clyde buffer rather than spent](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_18).""" ;
